issue.message:
Unexpected failure during lint analysis of BarChart.java (this is a bug in lint or one of the libraries it depends on)


The crash seems to involve the detector `com.greense.detector.mylibrary.ERBDetector`.
You can try disabling it with something like this:
    android {
        lintOptions {
            disable "Early Resource Binding"
        }
    }

Stack: `NullPointerException:Objects.requireNonNull(Objects.java:222)←ERBDetector$MyUElementHandler.visitField(ERBDetector.java:51)←UElementVisitor$DispatchPsiVisitor.visitField(UElementVisitor.kt:700)←UastVisitor$DefaultImpls.visitEnumConstant(UastVisitor.kt:33)←AbstractUastVisitor.visitEnumConstant(UastVisitor.kt:279)←UElementVisitor$DispatchPsiVisitor.visitEnumConstant(UElementVisitor.kt:673)←UElementVisitor$DelegatingPsiVisitor.visitEnumConstant(UElementVisitor.kt:1123)←UEnumConstant$DefaultImpls.accept(UVariable.kt:143)`

You can set environment variable `LINT_PRINT_STACKTRACE=true` to dump a full stacktrace to stdout.

